From 7888102ff7e43ed478b39192d02ec71c99462f85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:14:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] space: add common configuration of the capacity reported
 to clients

Motivation:
Doors report the size and free space of the storage to clients, e.g. to
df on an NFS mount, without a meaningful source: the NFS door reports a
fixed 1 EiB, and the xrootd door doesn't answer space queries at all.
Sites want to choose what is reported, and doors should agree on it.

Modification:
Add the dcache.capacity.source property with the values namespace (the
default, a fixed size as before), pools (the sum over all online pools,
computed as the frontend does for storage resource reporting) and
reservation (a space reservation), and the dcache.capacity.reservation
property for the space token of the reservation.

Add the Capacity class, which parses these properties and computes the
capacity of the pools or of a space reservation, for use by doors.

Result:
No change in behaviour. Doors can use a common configuration of the
capacity they report.

Target: master
Require-book: no
Require-notes: no
